// An orc shaman: an old orc, more bent than the others, its skin gone
// pale, under a great headdress of dark-teal and brown feathers and bone.
// Drawn from the user's reference (orc_shaman_ref.png) itself: its pixels
// read off at its own grid, shrunk to 0.70 (38 cells brow to sole, the
// headdress over that; then, bent, too big beside the player: the rows
// and columns that said least taken out, to 33), its colours clustered and lifted to read at night,
// cut into its head (the headdress, the amber eyes under a dark brow, the
// tusks, the jaw), its torso (the ragged teal robe, its hair hanging down
// its back in dark cords, a skull at its belt, a pouch), its far arm
// (bare, a brown wrap at the wrist, a hanging fist) and its near arm held
// out with the gnarled staff in its fist, forked at the head, cords and
// charms off it; the fire on the staff is a part of its own, put where the
// staff's head is in each pose (flickering, flaring as it casts): its core
// is the creature's `eyes` colour, so it glows in the dark as its eyes
// do. Its legs aren't drawn here: they're its creature file's `legs`
// (legs.rs, `rig`: wrapped shins and boots from under its hem), and its
// run keeps in step with them (`in_step`). Facing right; the game mirrors
// it.
(
    size: (54, 52),
    feet: (17.0, 52),
    outline: (14, 13, 8),
    palette: {
        'x': (14, 13, 8),           // the deepest shade
